   [
    "Class families",
    "<p>The sheet groups classes into five families, one per Beginner class; the divine classes also belong to one of them.</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"md\"><tr><th>Family</th><th>Beginner</th><th>Examples</th></tr><tr><td>Gladiators</td><td><a href=\"#/clase/JID_闘士\">Gladiator</a></td><td><a href=\"#/clase/JID_剣士\">Myrmidon</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_ブリガンド\">Brigand</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_セスタス\">Pugilist</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_ウォーリアー\">Warrior</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_踊り子\">Dancer</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_ソードマスター\">Swordmaster</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_バトルマスター\">Battlemaster</a></td></tr><tr><td>Hunters</td><td><a href=\"#/clase/JID_猟兵\">Hunter</a></td><td><a href=\"#/clase/JID_アーチャー\">Archer</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_ローグ\">Rogue</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_スナイパー\">Sniper</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_フォレストナイト\">Forest Knight</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_マスターアーチ\">Bow Adept</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_シャドーシーカー\">Shadow Seeker</a></td></tr><tr><td>Soldiers</td><td><a href=\"#/clase/JID_兵士\">Soldier</a></td><td><a href=\"#/clase/JID_重装歩兵\">Armored Knight</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_軽騎兵\">Light Cavalry</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_戦車兵\">Charioteer</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_ヘヴィアーマー\">Dreadnought</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_カタフラクト\">Cataphract</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_グレートナイト\">Great Knight</a></td></tr><tr><td>Fliers</td><td><a href=\"#/clase/JID_飛駝兵\">Ornius Rider</a></td><td><a href=\"#/clase/JID_騎甲駝兵\">Armored Ornius Rider</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_天翼兵\">Wing Soldier</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_カラドリオス\">Caladrius</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_ドラグーン\">Dragoon</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_ドラゴンマスター\">Bau Lord</a></td></tr><tr><td>Mages</td><td><a href=\"#/clase/JID_呪い師\">Diviner</a></td><td><a href=\"#/clase/JID_シャーマン\">Shaman</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_プリースト\">Priest</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_ウァテス\">Ovate</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_ビショップ\">Bishop</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_トルバドール\">Troubadour</a>, <a href=\"#/clase/JID_ヴァルキュリウム\">Valkyrium</a></td></tr></table></div>\n<p>On the sheet's Class tab, <b>\"Points to Master\"</b> says how much Class Exp is left to master the current class.</p>"
   ],
   [
    "Movement type",
    "<p>Each class has a movement type that sets how much each terrain costs it; the table of types and classes is in <a href=\"#/guia/terreno\">Terrain</a>.</p>"
   ],
   [
    "Why not repeat another Beginner class after mastering one",
    "<p>Once a Beginner class is mastered, moving to another Beginner class adds almost nothing: its mastery is +1 to one or two stats that rarely deserves a slot, its growths are low (+10 to two or three stats) and the exam costs a license, gold and a step of the <a href=\"#/guia/crecimientos\">fixed level-up sequence</a>. What pays off is staying in the Beginner class whose growths suit the unit and moving to a Specialty class as soon as you reach Renown 4 and the recommended level; from there, short visits to other Specialty classes for their mastery do pay off (<a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_好調\">Crescendo</a>, <a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_大反撃\">Great Counter</a>, <a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_技の冴え\">Ravaging Arts</a>).</p>"
   ],
   [
    "Min-max tips",
    "<ul>\n<li>Change on reaching 20, 35 and 45: every level spent in a lower-rank class is lost growth.</li>\n<li>Bridge classes for a weak stat: <a href=\"#/clase/JID_ブリガンド\">Brigand</a> (HP and Str +15), <a href=\"#/clase/JID_重装歩兵\">Armored Knight</a> (Def +25), <a href=\"#/clase/JID_シャーマン\">Shaman</a> (Mag +15), <a href=\"#/clase/JID_剣士\">Myrmidon</a> (Spd +15).</li>\n<li>Passing early works as a \"minimums exam\": the Armored Knight gifts Def to mages and the <a href=\"#/clase/JID_飛駝兵\">Ornius Rider</a>, Spd 8.</li>\n<li>Class Exp also rises with \"Training\" in Auto-Activities: you can master a bridge class without fighting in it.</li>\n<li>Each exam's result is fixed from the start of the chapter; with Restart Chapter and cheap filler exams you choose which attempt passes.</li>\n</ul>"
   ]
