  "tema": "combate",
  "secs": [
   [
    "Summary",
    "<ul>\n<li>An ability is a passive effect (Str +1, Avo +20 if the enemy is effective…) or an effect with a chance to activate.</li>\n<li>There are eight types: personal, class, master (from mastery), skill rank, mount, temporary Thermae ones, Blaze and Diadems.</li>\n<li>Personal and class abilities are fixed; master, skill-rank and Thermae abilities take equippable slots (see «Slots»).</li>\n<li>A mastered class's master ability is kept forever and can be equipped in any class.</li>\n<li>Combat Arts are something else: they are used from the menu and spend durability (see <a href=\"#/guia/tecnicas\">Combat Arts</a> and the tutorial <a href=\"#/tutorial/TUTO_戦技\">Combat Arts</a>).</li>\n</ul>"
   ],
   [
    "How it works",
    "<p>Each ability has a trigger and an effect. «Chance = X%» ones usually depend on a stat (Def/2%, Str/2%, Lck%). Proximity ones («to adjacent allies») also work in Dungeon Clashes. Flat bonuses from abilities, mount, battalion and dance share the <a href=\"#/guia/atributos-de-combate\">+10 cap</a> per stat.</p>"
   ],
   [
    "Slots",
    "<ul>\n<li>Each unit equips <b>up to 5 abilities</b> and, separately, <b>3 base Combat Arts</b>, plus any its class adds with Combat Arts +1/+2/+3 (up to 6).</li>\n<li>The <b>personal ability takes no slot</b>: it's always active and can't be swapped to another unit.</li>\n<li>Learned magic doesn't take a Combat Art slot either.</li>\n<li>Skill-rank abilities (Sword Lv 1, Bow Lv 1…) do take a slot, like master and Thermae abilities.</li>\n<li>They are changed in «Inventory», in the battle preparations or at the base. «Optimize Abilities» and «Optimize Combat Arts» pick them automatically, for one unit or for all.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The 5 slots fill up fast: avoid repeating the same ability across the whole team, and drop level 1 skill-rank abilities as soon as there's something better.</p>"
   ],
   [
    "Types",
    "<div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"md\"><tr><th>Type</th><th>How it's obtained</th><th>Equippable?</th></tr><tr><td>Personal</td><td>Each character's own; many improve at Lv 20 and Lv 35</td><td>Fixed</td></tr><tr><td>Class</td><td>While in the class</td><td>Fixed, changes with the class</td></tr><tr><td>Master</td><td>By mastering the class (Class Exp)</td><td>Yes, in any class and forever</td></tr><tr><td>Skill rank</td><td>On reaching certain ranks (Heavy Armor C: <a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_重装移動術\">Armored Move</a>; Infantry C: <a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_身躱し\">Dodge</a>…)</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Mount (Cai's route)</td><td>With enough bond with the animal being ridden</td><td>Chosen in Swap Spaces</td></tr><tr><td>Effect… (Thermae)</td><td>Bathing from Renown Lv 8; one at random from the bath</td><td>Yes, for the whole chapter</td></tr><tr><td>Blaze</td><td>Lords and some characters; they control the Blaze Gauge</td><td>Fixed (see <a href=\"#/guia/ignicion\">Blaze</a>)</td></tr><tr><td>Diadem</td><td>Innate activation of certain characters</td><td>Fixed (see <a href=\"#/guia/halos\">Diadems</a>)</td></tr></table></div>\n<p>Beginner class masteries are very small (<a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_攻撃の基本\">Attack Basics</a>: Str +1; <a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_狩猟の基本\">Hunting Basics</a>: Dex +1 and Spd +1). Specialty ones already change builds: <a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_好調\">Crescendo</a> (<a href=\"#/clase/JID_アーチャー\">Archer</a>, Hit +3 per kill up to +30 in that battle), <a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_大反撃\">Great Counter</a> (<a href=\"#/clase/JID_重装歩兵\">Armored Knight</a>, Atk +3 if the enemy attacks first) and <a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_脅威の察知\">Sense Threat</a> (<a href=\"#/clase/JID_騎甲駝兵\">Armored Ornius Rider</a>, Avo +20 against effective attacks). Among Advanced ones, <a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_熟練の技\">Practiced Art</a> (<a href=\"#/clase/JID_ウォーリアー\">Warrior</a>, Hit +10 with Combat Arts), <a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_残心\">Ever Vigilant</a> (<a href=\"#/clase/JID_シドー\">Shido</a>) and <a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_駆け抜け\">Overtake</a> (<a href=\"#/clase/JID_カラドリオス\">Caladrius</a>, Mov +1 per kill) stand out. Divine class ones (Part 3) give +10 to a stat.</p>"
   ],
   [
    "How to get them",
    "<ul>\n<li><b>Class mastery:</b> Class Exp fills the bar (how much each tier needs: <a href=\"#/guia/clases\">Classes</a>). It's earned in combat, on the map and with «Training» in the Inn's Auto-Activities, without fighting.</li>\n<li><b>Skill ranks:</b> each character has their own learning table by rank (on their sheet, Build tab).</li>\n<li><b>Mount (Cai's route):</b> see <a href=\"#/guia/monturas\">Mounts</a>; the ability becomes «+» at bond 5.</li>\n<li><b>Thermae:</b> each bath draws 1 of its 7–8 abilities; Sunday's special baths give «+» versions.</li>\n</ul>"
   ],
   [
    "Min-max tips",
    "<ul>\n<li>Master cheap classes with a good mastery early and go back to the main class: the mastery stays.</li>\n<li>On Hard, Hit matters more than damage: Crescendo, Practiced Art and <a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_射撃の達人\">Marksmanship</a> (<a href=\"#/clase/JID_スナイパー\">Sniper</a>, Hit +15 with bows) pay off a lot.</li>\n<li>A Beginner mastery (+1 to a stat) is rarely worth a slot.</li>\n<li>Some defensive personal abilities (<a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_力の大防御\">Strength Fend</a>, <a href=\"#/habilidad/SID_守護騎士の務め\">Guardian's Duty</a>) can be learned and equipped outside their original class<span class=\"gu-com\" title=\"Community fact\"><span class=\"sr-only\">(community fact)</span></span>.</li>\n</ul>"
   ]
  ]
